From d6a9d8fb2a9c0fa67487fbf8b4fe05f3a95029e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mohammed <91819504+mohammed7s@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:09:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Screen automation: let the user allow agents and target apps

With the user allowlists in frameworks/base, the screen automation pages
become the place where the user decides which apps may use screen
automation and which apps may be automated.

 - Special app access > Screen automation lists every app that holds
   ACCESS_COMPUTER_CONTROL (a privileged permission, so only preinstalled
   apps), not only those already allowed; unallowed ones read
   "Not allowed".
 - An agent's page gets a main switch, "Allow screen automation", off by
   default. The list of apps it may automate is disabled while it is off.
 - App info > Screen automation is shown for every launchable app that is
   not itself an agent. Its page gets a main switch, "Allow screen
   automation of this app", off by default.

Both switches only open a gate: the agent must still be the default
digital assistant, and each target still needs the user's approval in the
consent dialog. Turning a switch off closes the sessions that depend on
it.

